
is the single source of truth for warehouse database structure.

Never:

- Invent warehouse tables.
- Invent columns.
- Assume relationships.
- Create duplicate inventory structures.
- Modify warehouse logic without schema review.

---

# Warehouse Domain Scope

Warehouse domain may include:

- Warehouses
- Branch warehouses
- Products
- Categories
- Inventory balances
- Stock movements
- Receipts
- Deliveries
- Transfers
- Returns
- Serial numbers
- Batch numbers
- Inventory adjustments
- Warehouse locations

Always follow the existing schema.

---

# Entity Generation Rules

When generating warehouse entities:

- Match table names exactly.
- Match column names exactly.
- Preserve data types.
- Preserve nullable definitions.
- Create relationships based on relations.json.
- Apply constraints from schema.

---

# EF Core Mapping Rules

Always configure warehouse entities explicitly.

Example:

```csharp
builder.ToTable("InventoryTransactions");

builder.HasKey(x => x.Id);

builder.Property(x => x.Quantity)
       .HasColumnType("decimal(18,3)");